      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As described in the documentation:\n*Blendshape used when looking up/down-- use this to tweak eye/iris/lid/eyebrow positioning*\nYou can adjust anything in these blendshapes, and we found it works best when you use it to adjust eyebrow/eyelid position on your avatar. Depends very much on the style of your avatar. Anime-styled avatars won't have much to adjust, but other types of avatars may want to adjust eyelid movement to make looking up/down look more realistic-- hence the generic \"looking up\" and \"looking down\" blendshapes.\nThe documentation lays this out fairly flat.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-11T18:16:40.220Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "These blendshapes are intended to move the upper and lower eyelids depending on if your avatar is looking up or looking down, not blendshapes to make your eyes themselves look up or down.\nIdeally, these should be \"Eyelids [direction]\" or \"Eyelid look [direction]\" as to not be confused with eye positioning.",
